 "text": "Hi! How's life treating you? Not necessarily, it just few extra layers. Lots of cold guys on bikes because they' the most visible to traffic. Cover them with a light mesh or a sheet so they get some light. Cold air is worse for them. Buy winter gloves that keep the fingers together so they stay dry and you can still ride without them cutting off the blood. That's usually much safer. The roads can get quite rough too. Not necessarily, but deep rims might struggle if the ice is bad. A quiet push is always an option.",
